  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 6.9,
      "end": 14.34,
      "text": "On 275 and 285. Also in stereo on VHF. This is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.34,
      "end": 29.6,
      "text": "Well, hello there. This is TV on the Radio here, Thomas the Vance, and welcome once again to The Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.6,
      "end": 34.6,
      "text": "Just for the sound of it, tonight we repeat our 1981 session from Witchfind.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.6,
      "end": 42.6,
      "text": "And also, out of the archives, we revive a 1973 session by one of Ireland's finest, the rather great Rory Gallagher.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.48,
      "end": 61.26,
      "text": "And we've got some new stuff from Billy Squire, Rose Tattoo, Thin Lizzy, Gillan, Overdrive, Export and Caravan.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.2,
      "end": 67.22,
      "text": "Some classics via Jethro Tull, Pink Floyd, The Eagles, Bruford, Sammy Hagar and others.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.78,
      "end": 72.34,
      "text": "Plus, of course, the return of the Friday Night Connection and the outset of one of our fortnight ago.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.76,
      "end": 73.9,
      "text": "But tonight we start with this.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.77,
      "end": 85.71,
      "text": "I'm ready for you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 86.64,
      "end": 87.64,
      "text": "Are you ready for me?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 88.18,
      "end": 100.15,
      "text": "The fever of a love that burns.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 100.15,
      "end": 113.95,
      "text": "I don't know too much about that guy and his band at all, other than the fact that it's come out on Capitol.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.95,
      "end": 522.13,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 522.13,
      "end": 523.79,
      "text": "It's an album called Don't Say No.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 523.95,
      "end": 527.57,
      "text": "The man's name is Billy Squire, S-Q-U-I-E-R.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 528.94,
      "end": 536.54,
      "text": "And he's going to be on tour with a man called David Coverdale, along with Whitesnake, have you heard, with a track from their latest album called Come and Get It.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 536.9,
      "end": 540.52,
      "text": "The track that we played was Hot Stuff, and the Squire track was In the Dark.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 545.62,
      "end": 547.66,
      "text": "It's 11 minutes after 10.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 547.66,
      "end": 572.14,
      "text": "Old rock of war is here too long. War is round the corner, too tight.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 574.41,
      "end": 583.29,
      "text": "Unbatchable to the end. Drag is a hate to life.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 583.29,
      "end": 594.54,
      "text": "Dance headbound, fucker, yesterday's breeze. The crowd forget, rob it of you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 594.54,
      "end": 600.18,
      "text": "Ringing a change in his",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 600.18,
      "end": 603.7,
      "text": "Doubles her scenes in his",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 603.7,
      "end": 607.16,
      "text": "First one they give glitz",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 607.16,
      "end": 610.65,
      "text": "Silver",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 610.65,
      "end": 613.57,
      "text": "Rocker",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 613.57,
      "end": 616.85,
      "text": "Danny",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 616.85,
      "end": 623.06,
      "text": "Silver",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 623.06,
      "end": 629.17,
      "text": "Danny",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 629.17,
      "end": 635.15,
      "text": "Silver",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 635.15,
      "end": 636.81,
      "text": "Rocker",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 636.81,
      "end": 639.15,
      "text": "Gets out his bike",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 639.15,
      "end": 643.49,
      "text": "To make it time before he takes his leave",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 643.49,
      "end": 648.35,
      "text": "Up on the A1",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 648.35,
      "end": 651.39,
      "text": "By Scott's Corner",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 651.39,
      "end": 655.61,
      "text": "Just like it used to be",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 655.61,
      "end": 659.93,
      "text": "And as he flies",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 659.93,
      "end": 663.69,
      "text": "And tears in his eyes",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 663.69,
      "end": 665.09,
      "text": "In the wind, wind, wind",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 665.09,
      "end": 667.59,
      "text": "Echo the final take",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 667.59,
      "end": 671.91,
      "text": "And he hits the turnaround",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 671.91,
      "end": 682.71,
      "text": "soon to be seen again in our country i'm happy to say i hope i'm there every single",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 682.71,
      "end": 895.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 900.0,
      "end": 992.12,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 992.12,
      "end": 999.52,
      "text": "night that was specially from helen boswell who lives at 228 brown hill road catford london se6",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 999.52,
      "end": 1004.32,
      "text": "for a gentleman to whom she is affianced a gentleman by the name of jim warren",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1004.32,
      "end": 1007.38,
      "text": "who's having an enforced holiday at this moment in time.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1007.96,
      "end": 1009.96,
      "text": "But Jim, she still thinks highly of you.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1011.02,
      "end": 1014.28,
      "text": "Also played that fight track from Steve to Ian Thomas,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1014.66,
      "end": 1016.86,
      "text": "who's got a birthday coming up on the 25th of April.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1017.02,
      "end": 1018.36,
      "text": "On that day, he's going to be 18.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1020.85,
      "end": 1023.75,
      "text": "Before that, you heard Too Old to Rock and Roll and Too Young to Die.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1024.39,
      "end": 1027.45,
      "text": "Then the double album Live Bursting Out by Jethro Tull.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1028.68,
      "end": 1030.62,
      "text": "Lots of Jethro requests, as ever.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1031.14,
      "end": 1034.84,
      "text": "This one says say hi to my brothers Kenny and Richard Smith",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1034.84,
      "end": 1037.28,
      "text": "of [redacted address] in Dundee,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1037.46,
      "end": 1038.6,
      "text": "Ta from George Smith.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1040.56,
      "end": 1044.32,
      "text": "And also Hophead and Yoko from South Shields",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1044.32,
      "end": 1045.88,
      "text": "are well into Jethro Tull.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1047.96,
      "end": 1049.9,
      "text": "It's 10.20. Here's which find.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1050.38,
      "end": 1053.38,
      "text": "Collect your pennies,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1497.86,
      "end": 1500.68,
      "text": "because everybody says that band are well worth seeing.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1501.46,
      "end": 1502.7,
      "text": "At the moment, they're not in this country.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1502.8,
      "end": 1504.0,
      "text": "They actually come from Australia.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1504.2,
      "end": 1505.96,
      "text": "That album was laid out in 1978.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1506.16,
      "end": 1507.58,
      "text": "It's just been released over here.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1508.16,
      "end": 1510.36,
      "text": "It's by a band called Rose Tattoo.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1510.78,
      "end": 1513.22,
      "text": "The LP is called Rock and Roll Outlaw.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1513.22,
      "end": 1514.88,
      "text": "you just heard the title track of that",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1514.88,
      "end": 1517.32,
      "text": "and in about three weeks time you'll be able",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1517.32,
      "end": 1519.24,
      "text": "to hear a session that Tony Wilson laid down",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1519.24,
      "end": 1521.34,
      "text": "in the studios of the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1521.34,
      "end": 1523.42,
      "text": "BBC at Maida Vale just two nights",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1523.42,
      "end": 1527.74,
      "text": "ago, really is something",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1527.74,
      "end": 1528.96,
      "text": "worth waiting for",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1528.96,
      "end": 1532.01,
      "text": "and I think that band are going to be ginormous",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1532.01,
      "end": 1534.17,
      "text": "and prior to that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1534.17,
      "end": 1535.99,
      "text": "you heard something from our repeat session",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1535.99,
      "end": 1537.29,
      "text": "by the band called Witchvine",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1537.29,
      "end": 1539.85,
      "text": "it was the title track of their first album",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1539.85,
      "end": 1540.91,
      "text": "Give Them Hell",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1540.91,
      "end": 1546.22,
      "text": "the 5th of the 2nd",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1546.22,
      "end": 1548.56,
      "text": "1973, the BBC",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1548.56,
      "end": 1550.66,
      "text": "Studios, Rory Gallagher.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1550.66,
      "end": 2101.54,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1900.07,
      "end": 1906.07,
      "text": "And as they were, we're back in January, February 1973",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2101.54,
      "end": 2103.18,
      "text": "with Lou Martin on the keyboards.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2103.78,
      "end": 2108.09,
      "text": "And we have no idea what the title of that track is.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2108.25,
      "end": 2111.39,
      "text": "According to our records, it's just three exclamation marks.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2111.69,
      "end": 2113.85,
      "text": "Although somewhere down the line, I do recognize it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2113.85,
      "end": 2115.99,
      "text": "If you think you know what the title of that is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2116.49,
      "end": 2117.67,
      "text": "do me a favor and let us know.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2117.67,
      "end": 2124.07,
      "text": "will amend our records accordingly the track you heard before that by mr gallagher and his band",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2124.07,
      "end": 2130.47,
      "text": "was a track called hands off and there's a guy who's staying power in the business has",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2130.47,
      "end": 2145.56,
      "text": "been achieved purely by hard work lots of touring and pure talent this was recorded",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2145.56,
      "end": 2148.76,
      "text": "june 1980 in the beautiful city of dublin",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2148.76,
      "end": 2156.56,
      "text": "you've been out riding fences for so long now you're a hard one",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2410.54,
      "end": 2455.05,
      "text": "but you're only one of the ones",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2455.05,
      "end": 2465.25,
      "text": "was which fine from our session by them our repeat session by them the track was called",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2822.75,
      "end": 2828.69,
      "text": "moon magic and before that you heard desperado from the double album eagles live by the eagles",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2828.69,
      "end": 2833.27,
      "text": "prior to that something from a really good four tracker 12 inch at the sound of the moment",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2833.27,
      "end": 2839.49,
      "text": "killer's live ep it's called the track we played was are you ready also on that album or should i",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2839.49,
      "end": 2842.69,
      "text": "say EPR, Dear Miss Lonely Hearts, Opium Trail,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2843.01,
      "end": 2845.89,
      "text": "and an incredibly good version of Bad Reputation.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2847.76,
      "end": 2850.32,
      "text": "Thin Lizzy was most especially for a lady who's rather bored",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2850.32,
      "end": 2854.14,
      "text": "because of the moment she's down in a small, but I'm sure very beautiful village",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2854.14,
      "end": 2856.08,
      "text": "called Broad Windsor in Dawson.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2856.54,
      "end": 2861.26,
      "text": "She describes it as being a tiny village full of old ladies and miles from anywhere,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2861.26,
      "end": 2864.38,
      "text": "which gives her nothing to do all evening except listen to the radio.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2864.76,
      "end": 2865.88,
      "text": "Emma Thomas, how are you?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2865.88,
      "end": 2871.5,
      "text": "also played by Mark Flower",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2871.5,
      "end": 2874.18,
      "text": "at [redacted address] Southwich",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2874.18,
      "end": 2875.62,
      "text": "near Brighton",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2875.62,
      "end": 2879.17,
      "text": "I've got to mention a gentleman by the name of Studs",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2879.17,
      "end": 2881.29,
      "text": "it's his 22nd birthday",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2881.29,
      "end": 2883.71,
      "text": "on Monday the 27th of this month",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2883.71,
      "end": 2885.45,
      "text": "Sue Walsh",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2885.45,
      "end": 2887.71,
      "text": "a dear old Paddington London W9",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2887.71,
      "end": 2888.89,
      "text": "sends her love to you",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2888.89,
      "end": 2891.69,
      "text": "and says happy birthday for the 22nd",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2891.69,
      "end": 2899.48,
      "text": "birthday of yours on the 27th",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2899.48,
      "end": 2901.46,
      "text": "on Saturday at midday",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2901.46,
      "end": 2905.68,
      "text": "In the Steve Wright Show, you can hear part six of Star Wars.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2906.86,
      "end": 2917.7,
      "text": "Part six, the Millennium Falcon deal.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2918.18,
      "end": 2921.56,
      "text": "And our hero, Luke Skywalker, with Ben Obi-Wan Kenobi,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2921.98,
      "end": 2925.28,
      "text": "goes recruiting for assistance in a very dodgy bar.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2925.8,
      "end": 2928.98,
      "text": "Look at this place.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2929.61,
      "end": 2930.65,
      "text": "Oh, my goodness.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2931.21,
      "end": 2933.63,
      "text": "I've never seen so many non-humans in one place.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2934.46,
      "end": 2936.44,
      "text": "Look, there's a Myriad Hammerhead over there.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2937.37,
      "end": 2938.67,
      "text": "A Stofo Lupinoid.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2939.23,
      "end": 2941.41,
      "text": "Look, a couple of Tin Tin Dwarves.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2941.41,
      "end": 2943.73,
      "text": "R2, look. Even the humans don't look human.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2943.89,
      "end": 2946.79,
      "text": "This cantina is a meeting ground and a place of business",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2946.79,
      "end": 2949.11,
      "text": "for half the shady goings-on in this part of space.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2949.49,
      "end": 2952.27,
      "text": "Stay close to me. R2 and 3PO, you too.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2952.37,
      "end": 2952.99,
      "text": "Yes, sir.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2953.15,
      "end": 2956.23,
      "text": "To find out just who they recruit in that very doubtful bar,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2956.55,
      "end": 2961.65,
      "text": "listen in at 12 midday tomorrow for episode 6 of Star Wars.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2962.19,
      "end": 2967.59,
      "text": "For Future Shock, the track was Bite the Bullet.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2967.59,
      "end": 3269.92,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3269.92,
      "end": 3274.4,
      "text": "Gratifying it is to see that that album has gone into the BBC Top 30 album chart",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3274.4,
      "end": 3276.38,
      "text": "straight in at number two.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3278.0,
      "end": 3279.88,
      "text": "Ian and the rest of the band as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3280.16,
      "end": 3281.9,
      "text": "Incidentally, Ian Gillen is getting together",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3281.9,
      "end": 3283.54,
      "text": "a charity football match,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3283.62,
      "end": 3286.34,
      "text": "the exact location of which I'm not sure of,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3286.38,
      "end": 3290.0,
      "text": "but it's sort of up around exit 12 of the M4,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3290.18,
      "end": 3292.36,
      "text": "that type, or rather that part of the world.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3292.84,
      "end": 3295.24,
      "text": "It'll happen on the 3rd of May, Sunday the 3rd of May.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3295.32,
      "end": 3297.56,
      "text": "As soon as I get more details, I'll let you know,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3297.64,
      "end": 3299.72,
      "text": "because there's going to be a load of loonies on the field",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3299.72,
      "end": 3301.0,
      "text": "playing the football.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3302.69,
      "end": 3304.59,
      "text": "Many thanks to everybody who's phoned in",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3304.59,
      "end": 3307.41,
      "text": "and reminded us that the Rory Gallagher track",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3307.41,
      "end": 3310.0,
      "text": "that bore no title in our records",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3310.0,
      "end": 3313.1,
      "text": "is actually the track called Banker's Blues.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3313.7,
      "end": 3314.14,
      "text": "Thank you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3314.98,
      "end": 3320.42,
      "text": "Time for the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3320.5,
      "end": 3322.84,
      "text": "The last one we gave you was A Fortnight Ago,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3323.36,
      "end": 3324.78,
      "text": "and the tracks we played were",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3324.78,
      "end": 3326.84,
      "text": "Every Man Should Know,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3327.34,
      "end": 3329.54,
      "text": "Queenie, it's also a subtitle for that song,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3329.6,
      "end": 3330.64,
      "text": "it's by Blackfoot,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3331.37,
      "end": 3332.89,
      "text": "and it's off the album Tom Captain.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3334.0,
      "end": 3336.1,
      "text": "Insanity by the Tigers of Pantang,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3336.18,
      "end": 3338.1,
      "text": "off the album Wild Cat,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3338.1,
      "end": 3343.62,
      "text": "and cat scratch fever by ted nugent from the album of the same name simple one really just",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3343.62,
      "end": 3354.22,
      "text": "about everybody got it the answer was cat clever little felines the cleverest of all is the person",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3354.22,
      "end": 3359.9,
      "text": "that gets the 10 pound record token and that is glenn scrivener who lives in a house called",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3359.9,
      "end": 3365.42,
      "text": "yarak which is incidentally a swear word in turkish to the best of my recollection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3365.98,
      "end": 3372.14,
      "text": "yarak is at number 14 lower street sproughton ipswich in suffolk glenn you get yourself",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3372.14,
      "end": 3381.74,
      "text": "10 pound record token and this is mr scrivener's own friday night connection friday night connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4168.26,
      "end": 4173.86,
      "text": "of glenn scrivener who lives in sproggen in ipswich nice bit of boogie glenn you get yourself",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4173.86,
      "end": 4179.5,
      "text": "a 10 pound record token now do you think you know what the friday night connection is three bits of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4179.5,
      "end": 4183.86,
      "text": "music there's a theme definitely in there somewhere if you think you know what it is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4183.86,
      "end": 4189.08,
      "text": "jot it down on a postcard letter any form of communication you like and send it to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4189.08,
      "end": 4191.12,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4191.12,
      "end": 4192.88,
      "text": "The Friday Vox Show",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4192.88,
      "end": 4194.86,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4194.86,
      "end": 4198.14,
      "text": "London W1A4WW",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4198.14,
      "end": 4202.58,
      "text": "But don't forget to put together your own Friday Night Connection as well",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4202.58,
      "end": 4203.28,
      "text": "And good luck",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4203.28,
      "end": 4212.77,
      "text": "It's 11.12 and witch find are getting heavy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4212.77,
      "end": 4215.77,
      "text": "And they call themselves Overdrive",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4215.77,
      "end": 4631.77,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4636.77,
      "end": 4638.37,
      "text": "That track is called Nightmare",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4638.37,
      "end": 4640.37,
      "text": "One of three tracks on a single they've got out at the moment",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4640.37,
      "end": 4645.51,
      "text": "On the brilliantly named Boring Grantham record label",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4645.51,
      "end": 4648.49,
      "text": "I'd been to Grantham, I didn't think it was that boring",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4648.49,
      "end": 4651.45,
      "text": "Prior to that you heard Witchfind, our repeat session by then",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4651.45,
      "end": 4652.63,
      "text": "The track was called Gettin' Heavy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4652.63,
      "end": 4655.57,
      "text": "You'll find that recorded on their album Give Em Hell",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4655.57,
      "end": 4659.57,
      "text": "Back to February 1973 and more from Rory G",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4659.57,
      "end": 4667.97,
      "text": "That's Rory Gallagher out of the archives from the 5th of the 2nd, 1973",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4667.97,
      "end": 5455.51,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5455.51,
      "end": 5460.09,
      "text": "That was called Call Me The Breeze and before that you heard Walk On The Hot Coals",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5460.09,
      "end": 5462.93,
      "text": "And the band at that time were Jerry McAvoy on the bass",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5462.93,
      "end": 5464.51,
      "text": "Rod D'Arthur the drums",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5464.51,
      "end": 5466.45,
      "text": "and Lou Martin on the Joanna",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5466.45,
      "end": 5469.77,
      "text": "Incidentally, Lou Martin, who of course is an excellent pianist",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5469.77,
      "end": 5472.05,
      "text": "can be seen these days on Saturday nights",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5472.05,
      "end": 5474.13,
      "text": "at one of my favourite places in town",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5474.13,
      "end": 5476.81,
      "text": "It's a little wine bar by the name of Frogs",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5476.81,
      "end": 5479.43,
      "text": "spelt P-H, which is at the back of Olympia",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5479.43,
      "end": 5482.33,
      "text": "On Saturday nights, he hits the old Joanna, does Lou",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5482.33,
      "end": 5484.43,
      "text": "and Nicky Barkley, ex of Fanny",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5484.43,
      "end": 5486.21,
      "text": "does some really excellent singing",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5486.21,
      "end": 5487.37,
      "text": "Might even see you there",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5487.37,
      "end": 5500.36,
      "text": "This is a band called Export",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5500.36,
      "end": 5508.76,
      "text": "I tell you, the writer of that particular piece of music is Pye Hastings.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5895.24,
      "end": 5895.98,
      "text": "You'll know immediately.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5896.2,
      "end": 5897.58,
      "text": "It's the new single by Caravan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5898.2,
      "end": 5899.4,
      "text": "It's out on the Kingdom label.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5899.58,
      "end": 5901.4,
      "text": "It's called Keeping Up D-Fences.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5902.16,
      "end": 5905.27,
      "text": "And before that, a really good new single which is out on...",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5905.27,
      "end": 5906.15,
      "text": "Are you ready for this?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5906.47,
      "end": 5909.11,
      "text": "The His Master's Vice label.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5909.57,
      "end": 5912.13,
      "text": "It's by a tasty little band called Export.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5912.87,
      "end": 5915.36,
      "text": "And its title was You Gotta Rock.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5918.2,
      "end": 5920.18,
      "text": "Here's something we haven't played for quite some time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5920.36,
      "end": 5921.0,
      "text": "Tasty track.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5921.46,
      "end": 5923.54,
      "text": "Bill Bruford, Hell's Bells.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5923.84,
      "end": 5931.04,
      "text": "That was our repeat session by Witchfind, a nice session by them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5931.04,
      "end": 6467.94,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6467.94,
      "end": 6471.44,
      "text": "Chalky White on the vocals, Montalo, I think it is, on the guitar,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6471.64,
      "end": 6474.58,
      "text": "Peach Sir G on the bass and also backing vocals,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6475.08,
      "end": 6477.82,
      "text": "and Grace Scoresby on the drums.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6478.12,
      "end": 6480.22,
      "text": "That track was called Belfast.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6480.22,
      "end": 6483.34,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Bill Bruford from the album One of a Kind.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6483.6,
      "end": 6485.12,
      "text": "The track you heard was Hell's Bells.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6485.4,
      "end": 6487.8,
      "text": "Also incorporated the keyboard talent of Dave Stewart,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6488.26,
      "end": 6490.8,
      "text": "who's currently got a hit single along with Colin Blundstone,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6490.9,
      "end": 6491.76,
      "text": "which I'm happy to note.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6491.8,
      "end": 6499.54,
      "text": "And I played that specially for Graham, Graham Smith, that is, who will be 22 on May the 1st.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6499.58,
      "end": 6505.34,
      "text": "Okay, I'd like now to dedicate the next track that I'm going to play to a young lady who's going to be 16.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6505.76,
      "end": 6508.2,
      "text": "In fact, she is, as of midnight last night.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6508.86,
      "end": 6511.7,
      "text": "Her name is Sandra Johnson. She lives in Barnsley.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6512.16,
      "end": 6513.48,
      "text": "So does Ian, her boyfriend.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6514.18,
      "end": 6517.14,
      "text": "Ian Micklethwaite sends you lots and lots of love, Sandra.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6517.74,
      "end": 6520.2,
      "text": "And we play you this, the Young Girl Blues.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6520.2,
      "end": 6647.32,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6604.29,
      "end": 6619.5,
      "text": "Continue your way through the phonies.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6619.94,
      "end": 6633.35,
      "text": "My baby.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6647.32,
      "end": 6648.12,
      "text": "Stay safe.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6648.54,
      "end": 6655.74,
      "text": "From a chap who says he has not yet got a girlfriend.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7082.01,
      "end": 7083.19,
      "text": "That's Simon Kemp.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7083.81,
      "end": 7085.95,
      "text": "He lives at number four, Paddock Close in Oxford.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7086.19,
      "end": 7086.93,
      "text": "Get round there, girl.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7087.87,
      "end": 7089.97,
      "text": "Tomorrow on Rock On, between 5 and 6.30,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7090.07,
      "end": 7092.43,
      "text": "Wishbone Ash and The Scars.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7092.65,
      "end": 7094.07,
      "text": "Next week, we have Dead Ringer,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7094.19,
      "end": 7096.55,
      "text": "their first ever Friday rock show session.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7097.62,
      "end": 7099.18,
      "text": "Mr. Wilson, Tony Wilson,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7099.18,
      "end": 7101.18,
      "text": "Come here, come here, lazy devil.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7101.28,
      "end": 7101.8,
      "text": "Yes, what do you want?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7101.8,
      "end": 7102.76,
      "text": "I've got a pound here.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7102.84,
      "end": 7106.64,
      "text": "It's been sent in by Simon Kemp for any charity of our choice.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7107.02,
      "end": 7107.9,
